      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is too late, let\u0027s make this POST_KERNEL 50 or something.\n\nThe reason is because other system_init might actually call into i2c peripherals to set stuff up (like CBI EEPROM access to determine which SKU the device is).\n\nIf upstream already doesn\u0027t have one, it would probably be worth while to create a tool that printed out every sys_init and their corresponding priority to ensure from a birds eye view that it was all sequenced correctly (this would be a low prioirty task -- can you open a low priority issue to track this tool?)",
      "range": {
