      "writtenOn": "2020-11-02T16:10:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s shim in irq_lock into interrupt enabled/disable instead; otherwise we are going to have to change a decent amount of code\n\nI don\u0027t think that our current platofrm/ec code ever nest the interrupts more than 2 or 3 levels. We could implement disabled_interrupts to call irq_lock and save the key in a static buffer[4] then unwind with the appropriate irq_key in interrupt_enable. Platform/ec is already trying to move to nestable interreupt enable/diable calls",
      "range": {
